From 18beed2e13759b9b8cae5b69841b1e7a0540643a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Afonso <afonsofernando051@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:47:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pet): add contract-compliant wolf.riv companion

Adds assets/rive/pet/wolf.riv, the first pet built directly against the
Companion contract that PetRiveCompanion's default _CompanionRig expects:
artboard "Wolf", state machine "Companion", inputs state (PetAnimationState
index), reducedMotion (static pose per state) and interacting (medallion
pulse). No Dart changes are needed: wolf is not in _kRigForSpecie.

The file is generated reproducibly from assets/images/generated_wolf.png
by tools/rive_pet (slice -> 21 layers, build -> .riv) and was verified
with the official rive-runtime via a small C++ harness: loads, exposes
the expected state machine and inputs, static poses don't move under
reducedMotion, and every state returns cleanly to idle. Type/property
keys were cross-checked against rive 0.13.20, the runtime the app pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NQZcr29rrVaDqjp5ujTzTx
